  node [
    id 53
    label "BzbbqGY-aJU"
    step 0
    date "2020-07-26T12:18:02Z"
    title "#IndietracksAtHome: Chemtrails"
    description "Chemtrails began as the lo-fi bedroom recording project of romantic partners Mia Lust and Laura Orlova, evolving into a 5-piece garage-punk and acid-corroded new-wave outfit in  2016. Soon after, Chemtrails were signed by Swedish label PNKSLM Recordings, and have since gained a reputation for their prolific DIY output and high energy live shows. The band&#8217;s biggest influences are the Pixies, Blondie, Oh Sees, Black Lips and sixties psych and garage punk, but holding everything together is an ear for melody and no shortage of hooks, with cryptic lyrics that center around alienation, love, the human condition, the impending apocalypse and occasionally on Mia Lust&#8217;s place in the world as a transgender woman.  &#10;&#10;&#10;Support Chemtrails here: https://adoseofchemtrails.bandcamp.com/&#10;&#10;This video is presented as part of #IndietracksAtHome, a weekend of virtual events to bring together some of the artists, DJs and workshops that would have featured at Indietracks Festival 2020 (http://www.indietracks.co.uk).&#10;&#10;Indietracks Festival is a charity fundraiser for  the Midland Railway - Butterley, a heritage railway in the Derbyshire countryside. The railway relies on visitors for its income and has been closed for three months due to the coronavirus outbreak. You can support them by buying a compilation from a past edition of Indietracks Festival (https://indietracks.bandcamp.com/) or sending them a Paypal donation (https://www.paypal.com/gb/fundraiser/charity/140525)."
    channeltitle "Indietracks Festival"
    channelid "UCeaD-7v7d0tLRcc9ngaR5tw"
    favcount 0
    viewcount 1533
    likecount 36
    commentcount 3
    duration "PT8M3S"
    indegree 1
