    title "Convergence number 15 Chemtrails. Jet contrails. Geoengineering. Urban Heat Island and Moore F5"
    description "#california  #drought #lakemead #lakepowell #lakeshasta #lakeoroville #calfire #Washburnefire #dixiefire #carrfire #campfire #chemtrails #contrails #geoenginering #lakemead Albert Einstein once stated among the most difficult problems in all of physics was the earth's magnetic field.  I,  Michael Doran, a California attorney, argue that the earth's magnetic field is among the most difficult problems in all of BIOLOGY.  Quoting from PBS Nova article about contrails from 9/11 studies a state of the science is described.  The biggest mistake about chemtrails or jet contrails debate is that carbonation concentrated in exhaust from jets has a signal to it compared to just water vapor and the ambient amount of carbonation in the winds and typical clouds and what impact will be if the contrail or chemtrail will dissipate or grow into a weather changing cloud.  No need to talk conspiracy theory to add cloud seeding chemicals into the discussion.  If a cloud comes from a hurricane the surface low stirs and depressurizes the ocean there will be a carbonation signal.  If the cloud comes from a volcanic eruption the cloud will have a signal of carbonation and even sulfur.  What contrails or chemtrails have already is a signal of carbonation and sometimes sulfates depending on the fuel.  No need for secret additives. These contrails will already have the necessary carbonation to phase change in a signaling way to ice crystals in the context of electrical fields.  Once again, the state of the science looks at whether light is blocked or trapped as a greenhouse gas when the electrical and biological complexity of climate change makes jet contrails and chemtrails a different problem and makes it much less likely that governments are behind it, conspiring.  Urban areas can also have a carbonation signal, which makes, for example, the TWO Moore Oklahoma F5 tornadoes that CURVED around that urban area during rush hour interesting. It's when exhaust from cars in the sprawling urban area of Oklahoma City interesting, just like the exhaust from jets."
